{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01241",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 4.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Morning, come on through. Did you come far?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.47,
      "end_seconds": 10.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Not too far, about half an hour by bus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.88,
      "end_seconds": 13.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.74,
      "end_seconds": 22.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Yeah, um, it's sharp pain low on one side. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.29,
      "end_seconds": 27.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.59,
      "end_seconds": 34.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Well, um, I've had it for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.66,
      "end_seconds": 45.26,
      "duration_seconds": 10.6,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. So, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.96,
      "end_seconds": 60.72,
      "duration_seconds": 13.76,
      "text": "Um, I'd say once or twice a day. A seven out of ten, I suppose. Ah, I've also had shoulder tip pain, since Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.6,
      "end_seconds": 69.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "Have you had sharp pain low on one side before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.51,
      "end_seconds": 82.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.77,
      "text": "Yes, you know, something like this happened last winter, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.94,
      "end_seconds": 87.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "A few quick ones: fever or vaginal discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.04,
      "end_seconds": 92.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Nope, um, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.87,
      "end_seconds": 97.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.48,
      "end_seconds": 100.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.98,
      "end_seconds": 104.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.71,
      "end_seconds": 106.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.02,
      "end_seconds": 119.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.3,
      "end_seconds": 134.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.9,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.73,
      "end_seconds": 151.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.78,
      "end_seconds": 156.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "It's allopurinol, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.45,
      "end_seconds": 159.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.79,
      "end_seconds": 164.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "It's 100 milligrams. Febuxostat I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.93,
      "end_seconds": 169.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.48,
      "end_seconds": 172.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Yes, gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.28,
      "end_seconds": 176.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Okay, have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.65,
      "end_seconds": 180.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.24,
      "end_seconds": 184.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.19,
      "end_seconds": 195.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Right, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.62,
      "end_seconds": 216.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 116 beats a minute, temperature is 36.7 degrees. And SpO2 97 percent on room air, pressure 116 over 85."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.08,
      "end_seconds": 222.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.72,
      "end_seconds": 224.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.21,
      "end_seconds": 236.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Your tummy is tender low on the right and you look pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.83,
      "end_seconds": 239.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.95,
      "end_seconds": 258.26,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed. So where does that leave us? I think we're dealing with a possible ectopic pregnancy at this stage. I'd also keep a ruptured ovarian cyst in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.54,
      "end_seconds": 261.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.32,
      "end_seconds": 271.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a possible ectopic pregnancy is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.76,
      "end_seconds": 324.25,
      "duration_seconds": 36.49,
      "text": "We should do an urgent pelvic scan for possible ectopic. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I think a pregnancy test makes sense here, for pelvic pain and bleeding. You need to go to the hospital now for an emergency scan. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I'll want another look straight away. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.65,
      "end_seconds": 328.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}